{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Guard for yourself.</b> In my opinion, He is speaking with Moses, that he should guard these things and recount them thus to the children of Israel, in the manner of שמרו עדותיו וחוק נתן למו (Psalms 99:7), as I explained in its place." "And the beginning of the passage is that you shall say to them: הנני גרש מפניך, and this passage resembles the passage הנה אנכי שולח מלאך (above 23:20), with the passage that is above." "<b>And the word גרש.</b> From the binyan kal, and it is a transitive verb, and similarly אלמנה וגרושה (Leviticus 21:14)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:13.866172948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}